  "content": {
    "title": "Kansas basketball vs Cal Baptist final score: KU advances to Round of 32",
    "text": "March 20, 2026Updated March 21, 2026, 12:08 a.m. CTSAN DIEGO, California — Kansas basketball’s men’s NCAA tournament run started out Friday against California Baptist in San Diego, California, and saw the Jayhawks escape with a 68-60 win.The Jayhawks and Lancers met up in a round of 64 contest that saw Kansas lead by 20 points at halftime, before California Baptist roared back in the second half. Kansas, the No. 4 seed in the East Region, narrowly avoided an upset at the hands of No. 13 seed California Baptist.The Lancers pulled on the energy from an electric crowd, with California Baptist's Dominique Daniels Jr. nearly willing his team to a win against Kansas and Darryn Peterson.Watch Kansas basketball in March MadnessHere is what happened at Viejas Arena: UPDATE: 11:13 p.m. (CT): FINAL: Kansas 68, California Baptist 60 UPDATE: 10:59 p.m. (CT): Kansas leads 66-53 with 3:34 left in 2nd HalfKansas hasn't scored in more than two minutes, and that's helped allow California Baptist to make this a 13-point game with about three and a half minutes left in regulation. Dominique Daniels Jr. had been the catalyst of this comeback attempt for the Lancers, and is now at 20 points. Fifteen of those points have come in the second half. UPDATE: 10:44 p.m. (CT): Kansas leads 64-42 with 8:42 left in 2nd HalfDarryn Peterson just hit back-to-back 3s for Kansas, as he now sits at 26 points for the game. California Baptist's fans in the arena still have some life, but their Lancers are running out of time. KU is up 22 points with a little less than nine minutes left in regulation, and the Jayhawks have been coasting through much of this second half. UPDATE: 10:36 p.m. (CT): Kansas leads 54-31 with 12:14 left in 2nd HalfBryson Tiller is nearing a double-double for the Jayhawks, as he currently sits at six points and 10 rebounds. The only two KU players in double figures scoring are Darryn Peterson with 20 points, and Tre White with 10. California Baptist is going to need to start hitting some 3s if it's going to mount a comeback, but right now the Lancers are shooting 1-for-11 from behind the arc. UPDATE: 10:27 p.m. (CT): Kansas leads 48-22 with 15:51 left in 2nd HalfDarryn Peterson appeared to inadvertently get hit in the face during this recent stretch of play, but he remained in the game after appearing to be in pain in what'll be a positive sign for the Jayhawks. Kansas now leads by 26 points, tied for its largest lead of the game, with a little less than 16 minutes left in regulation. It'll be interesting to follow how long Kansas keeps its starters in the game, with what'll likely be a tough matchup against St. John's waiting on Sunday. UPDATE: 9:49 p.m. (CT): HALFTIME: Kansas 38, California Baptist 18 UPDATE: 9:46 p.m. (CT): Kansas leads 27-16 with 4:24 left in 1st HalfNeither team has been able to hit a 3-pointer yet tonight, with the Jayhawks shooting 0-for-3 and the Lancers at 0-for-6. Neither squad has seen their main option offensively enjoy much success at all so far, either. Darryn Peterson has six points so far for Kansas, and Dominique Daniels Jr. three for California Baptist, as both have struggled to hit shots from the field. UPDATE: 9:33 p.m. (CT): Kansas leads 23-8 with 9:05 left in 1st HalfKansas' Paul Mbiya just threw down a dunk for his first points of the game, as the Jayhawks take a 15-point lead with close to nine minutes left until halftime. Mbiya might not usually have been someone coach Bill Self would turn toward for pivotal first half minutes this season, but given the size California Baptist has inside he's needed right now if the Jayhawks are going to take one of either Flory Bidunga or Bryson Tiller out and go to the bench. UPDATE: 9:26 p.m. (CT): Kansas leads 13-5 with 11:40 left in 1st HalfIt's continued to be a poor shooting effort from both sides, with Kansas at 2-for-15 from the field and California Baptist at 2-for-12. The Jayhawks have an advantage, in large part, because they're shooting 9-for-10 from the free throw line. The Lancers are 1-for-4 from the free throw line. UPDATE: 9:16 p.m. (CT): Kansas leads 8-3 with 15:52 left in 1st HalfThe shots haven't been falling for either side all that much so far, but the Jayhawks have still been able to take an 8-3 lead with a little less than 16 minutes remaining in the first half. KU's Darryn Peterson has two points, but that's from the free throw line as he's 0-for-4 shooting from the field. California Baptist has already turned the ball over four times already, and that's led to six points for Kansas.PregameHere are the starting lineupsKansas coach Bill Self previews gameHere's the new tip-off timeWhy Samis Calderon won't be with Kansas basketball tonightKansas basketball vs California Baptist game timeDate: Friday, March 20Time: 8:45 p.m. (CT)Location: Viejas Arena in San Diego, CaliforniaWhat channel is Kansas basketball vs California Baptist on today?TV channel: CBSStreaming: FuboRadio: Jayhawk Radio NetworkKansas basketball’s game against California Baptist will be broadcast on CBS. Streaming options include Fubo. The winner of this game advances to the round of 32 of the NCAA tournament.Kansas basketball vs California Baptist betting lineOdds courtesy of FanDuel as of Thursday, March 19Spread: Kansas by 14.5O/U: 137.5Kansas basketball 2025-26 scheduleHere’s a look at Kansas’ last three games:March 7 (home): Kansas State — Kansas won 104-85March 12 (neutral): TCU — Kansas won 78-73March 13 (neutral): Houston — Kansas lost 69-47California Baptist 2025-26 scheduleHere’s a look at California Baptist’s last three games:March 7 (away): Southern Utah University — California Baptist won 82-75March 13 (neutral): Utah Tech — California Baptist won 86-72March 14 (neutral): Utah Valley University — California Baptist won 63-61Kansas basketball vs California Baptist scoreJordan Guskey covers University of Kansas Athletics at The Topeka Capital-Journal. He was the 2022 National Sports Media Association’s sportswriter of the year for the state of Kansas. Contact him at jmguskey@gannett.com or on Twitter at @JordanGuskey.We occasionally recommend interesting products and services. If you make a purchase by clicking one of the links, we may earn an affiliate fee. USA TODAY Network newsrooms operate independently, and this doesn’t influence our coverage.",
